{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/931185-clarification-about-the-beatdown-condition","id":931185,"title":"Clarification about the Beatdown condition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-13T21:59:33-07:00","id":931185,"title":"Clarification about the Beatdown condition?","content":"I need some clarification on the beatdown rule, following an encounter in my group's most recent session. I'll explain the situation, and hope to get a clearer understanding of how it should have resolved (and hopefully I explain this clearly):<br /> <br /> We have Characters A, a vampire with low Humanity (certainly he has no qualms with committing murder), attacking Character B.<br /> <br /> Character B, however, hits Character A with more damage than his Stamina, thus giving him the beatdown condition. At this point, if Character B states he just wants Character A to get lost, the conflict is resolved by Character A fleeing, correct? Or is character A immune to beatdown because he's too low humanity? I would think Humanity only applies to Character B, to ignore the effect of Character A's condition.<br /> <br /> Would anyone mind running through this with me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","user":"Blitzburger","date":". 07-14-2016, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T00:25:47-07:00","id":931227,"title":"","content":"If murder would not be a Breaking Point for character A, character A does not gain the Beaten Down Tilt and can continue to attack character B without spending Willpower or facing a Breaking Point, even if character B surrenders. However, character A is still free to surrender to character B if he feels the fight is going poorly for him and he doesn't want to draw it out any longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T01:55:07-07:00","id":931249,"title":"","content":"Here is a situation that occurred the other evening during a Vampire R2nd session that I was hoping the community could offer some clarification on: <br /> <br /> A vampire <u>(Named H) with a humanity of 6</u> was in a sewer and was attacked by <u>two other humanity 1 vampires</u>. As the fight broke out the humanity 1 vampires tried to kill 'H' but missed and were unsuccessful in their attacks... Before long Vampire 'H' hit one (then the other) doing <i>3bashing damage </i>(more than its stamina) to each of them. So we played that the humanity 1 monstrous vampires incurred the 'beat down' condition and surrendered to 'H' (the low humanity vampires then ran away) however, I feel that this was incorrect. It seems to me that the beat down condition is connected to a characters humanity and these nasty low humanity vampires likely should have been able to keep fighting.. I know that a character cannot get the beat down condition when he is fighting for his life but it seems as though the low humanity vampires would have also been exempt. Please clarify where this went wrong...if it did.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2600-vruffolo","name":"vruffolo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T02:29:20-07:00","id":931252,"title":"","content":"The Beat Down subsystem does clarify that if a being wouldn't take a breaking point for killing someone, they can't normally be affected by the Beaten Down tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T04:20:55-07:00","id":931268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/931185-clarification-about-the-beatdown-condition?p=931227#post931227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If murder would not be a Breaking Point for character A, character A does not gain the Beaten Down Tilt and can continue to attack character B without spending Willpower or facing a Breaking Point, even if character B surrenders. However, character A is still free to surrender to character B if he feels the fight is going poorly for him and he doesn't want to draw it out any longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>As ill adviced as surrender is to a murderer...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T05:26:39-07:00","id":931284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/931185-clarification-about-the-beatdown-condition?p=931268#post931268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As ill adviced as surrender is to a murderer...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, since in the example all character B wants is to make character A leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T05:57:53-07:00","id":931296,"title":"","content":"Of course, even at Humanity 1, &quot;heinous, spree, and mass murder&quot; is a Breaking Point. So at that point, some forms of murder constitute a breaking point and others don't. It's kind of an ST call if they should suffer Beaten Down or not. If they also remove &quot;heinous, spree, and mass murder&quot; as a Breaking Pony with a Bane though, then they're definitely immune to the Tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T05:59:51-07:00","id":931301,"title":"","content":"To add to my previous comment, even at Humanity 1, &quot;heinous, spree, and mass murder&quot; is a Breaking Point for vampires. So at that point, some forms of murder might constitute a breaking point and others might not. It's kind of an ST call if they should suffer Beaten Down or not while certain forms of murder are still Breaking Points. If they also remove &quot;heinous, spree, and mass murder&quot; as a Breaking Point with a Bane though, then they're definitely immune to the Tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T06:27:10-07:00","id":931312,"title":"","content":"If these two NPCs had planned to ambush this character expecting an easy kill only to both promptly get their asses handed to them, why exactly would they not flee at the first opportunity? It makes no sense for them to hang around waiting to get killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 07-14-2016, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T08:01:45-07:00","id":931359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/931185-clarification-about-the-beatdown-condition?p=931312#post931312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If these two NPCs had planned to ambush this character expecting an easy kill only to both promptly get their asses handed to them, why exactly would they not flee at the first opportunity? It makes no sense for them to hang around waiting to get killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I see it too.<br /> <br /> Can anyone explain to me the logic of having humanity have any bearing at all on whether a defender is beatdown or not? Why would low Humanity indicate any less of a survival instinct?<br /> <br /> BTW, sorry this topic was posted twice. Maybe the thread could be merged?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","user":"Blitzburger","date":". 07-14-2016, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T08:16:09-07:00","id":931366,"title":"","content":"Remember that depending on your Chronicle, you might be better off without the mechanic. Could someone with better English and less insomnia explain what is the purpose of Beaten Down from design and game mastering point of view?<br /> In general, certain conflicts benefit greatly from including Beaten Down, while others don't. I also hazily remember that we either increased the BDown bar for the vampires, or made it so that you could purge the damage with blood healing before game &quot;checked&quot; for being Beaten Down.<br /> EDIT<br /> Ah, we increased it to &quot;Stamina in Lethal&quot; Damage for creatures that can rapid heal as a part of their template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-14-2016, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T09:17:01-07:00","id":931403,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I understand it's an optional rule, but I also really like it. I just don't understand why people with no Humanity aren't subject to &quot;holy shit, THAT hurt ALOT. Here, take whatever you want, just don't hurt me&quot;. An analogy I like to use is smacking a shark in it's snout.<br /> <br /> I'm just thinking a house rule is in order, but I feel like I'm missing some perspective on this tilt, and want to understand it before making changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T09:25:09-07:00","id":931405,"title":"","content":"The mechanic is really only supposed to be considered when all sides of a fight don't really want to kill each other. Just because your Humanity rating is 2, that doesn't mean the character murders everyone at the slightest inclination. It means they aren't going to go crying in the corner IF they kill someone. Nor does it mean the high Humanity character won't put a bullet in their attackers' brains when they get jumped by three knife wielding killers. Tying the tilt to Humanity does nothing except provide an irrelevant and undeserved combat advantage against the high Humanity character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T09:56:37-07:00","id":931426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/931185-clarification-about-the-beatdown-condition?p=931359#post931359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone explain to me the logic of having humanity have any bearing at all on whether a defender is beatdown or not? Why would low Humanity indicate any less of a survival instinct?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much a matter of lacking survival instinct as it is a desensitization to violence. These characters are still perfectly capable of deciding &quot;hey, this guy is a lot tougher than we expected him to be, and just wants to be left alone. Let's do that.&quot; They even gain a point of Willpower for surrendering in that way. They just don't get the fight knocked out of them to the point where even defending themselves takes significant effort and costs Willpower.<br /> <br /> Also, I would argue that Humanity loss alone isn't enough to inure anyone short of Draughur to Beaten Down. As I mentioned, since &quot;heinous, spree, or mass murder&quot; is a Breaking Point right down to Humanity 1, I would personally rule that they're still subject to the Tilt. Unless they get rid of that one last qualm about killing with a Bane. And at that point I'd say they're sufficiently alien that it makes sense for them to be able to shrug off a savage beating.<br /> <br /> Since you asked in your other post, I believe that's the philosophy behind certain characters being immune to Beaten Down. In a game where ordinary people confront actual monsters, it's thematically appropriate for the monsters to take no quarter and fight to their last breath. It would be pretty weird if the slavering, bloodthirsty beast turned tail after being punched a few times, or couldn't bring themselves to continue tearing into their prey when it surrendered. &quot;Doesn't consider murder a Breaking Point&quot; happens to be the standard metric in CofD for when you cross the line from person to monster.<br /> <br /> And again, these characters aren't mindless. They can still make the rational decision that a fight isn't going in their favor and the most prudent course of action is to just give the other party what they want and walk away from the conflict. But if they're inhuman enough that they would have no compunctions about killing their victim if the tables were turned, they are also inhuman enough that they never reach the point where they <i>can't</i> fight back. Surrender becomes a choice, rather than something they do because they can't take any more beatings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/931185-clarification-about-the-beatdown-condition?p=931359#post931359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, sorry this topic was posted twice. Maybe the thread could be merged?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can do!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-14-2016, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:39:08-07:00","id":931453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/931185-clarification-about-the-beatdown-condition?p=931403#post931403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I understand it's an optional rule, but I also really like it. I just don't understand why people with no Humanity aren't subject to &quot;holy shit, THAT hurt ALOT. Here, take whatever you want, just don't hurt me&quot;. An analogy I like to use is smacking a shark in it's snout.<br /> <br /> I'm just thinking a house rule is in order, but I feel like I'm missing some perspective on this tilt, and want to understand it before making changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely sure either why vampires, who can shrug off incredible quantities of injury, without even spending Vitae to properly heal, would surrender so readily at what constitutes a series of smacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:44:00-07:00","id":931456,"title":"","content":"You might limit it so that it only comes into play if the damage is Lethal or higher.<br /> <br /> Granted it's something a vampire can survive, but taking a lot of Lethal in one shot is still going to be jarring for your average vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T12:15:04-07:00","id":931508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/931185-clarification-about-the-beatdown-condition?p=931456#post931456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might limit it so that it only comes into play if the damage is Lethal or higher.<br /> <br /> Granted it's something a vampire can survive, but taking a lot of Lethal in one shot is still going to be jarring for your average vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I do. Since vampires effectively treat most lethal damage as bashing and most agg damage as lethal, I just upgrade the requirements so it takes lethal &gt; Stamina or any amount of agg to Beat Down a vampire. Again, unless they have low humanity and/or Banes removing any Breaking Points related to killing, in which case they don't get Beaten Down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T16:58:41-07:00","id":931691,"title":"","content":"Also, remember that Beaten Down creatures can also spend Willpower to do aggressive action. This might lead into interesting situation where you get Beaten Down first, but you use your remaining Willpower to strike back, Beat Down your opponent, and neither of you can pursue your goals.<br /> It helps introduce one of concepts of &quot;how to survive while being weak&quot; - weaklings don't need to be strong enough to kill their opponents to be safe. They need to be strong enough to make taking them down so taxing, that aggressor will be weakened enough to be easy prey for *other* predators, which ends up in a stalemate.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Basically, here are possible resolutions for a conflict using Beaten Down, assuming both sides are capable of getting Tilted:<br /> <br /> 1. ONE SIDE SURRENDERS<br /> To achieve this, you need to do three things: deal enough damage to the target in order to inflict the Tilt, then weather down it's Willpower points so it can't take aggressive actions, and prevent it's escape route. Last two are optional, as they might concede early. You get what you wanted.<br /> <br /> 2. ONE SIDE ESCAPES<br /> No one surrenders. This usually is a case when someone decides to leg it and runs away; for example, you got Beaten Down and decided that you aren't beaten up good enough to surrender but also aren't in position to aim for stalemate or win, so you jump out of the window.<br /> <br /> 3. BOTH SIDES ARE UNABLE TO PURSUIT THEIR GOALS<br /> This can happen when both sides get Beaten Down; it's possible that person that got beaten down first might use their Willpower to make their opponent Beaten Down too. If both guys run out of Willpower before forcing the other party to submit, they can't take aggressive actions, so neither of them can pursue their goals and force the other side to surrender. So they both run away.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Accidentally, this skews chances towards player characters a lot, because they will usually be able to muster more Willpower than npcs, due to the guideline that npc characters should get 1, 2 Willpower points per scene at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-14-2016, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}